Fryeburg best known building is an  imposing one Freiburg Minster the city's  Cathedral the church's spire has been  described as the most beautiful on earth  and the city wants it to stay that way  despite Allied air raids during world  war ii the tower survived the Minster is  a masterpiece of Gothic architecture  built between the 13th and 16th  centuries many of the windows date back  to that time  in the center is the striking altar by  the Renaissance painter Hans balding  green pupil of the renowned artist all  brushed durum the interior of the  cathedral is decorated with numerous  panels sculptures and other beautiful  art treasures  Freiburg is known for another notable  feature The Bachelor or little Brooks  the network of tiny streams runs for  several kilometers through the center of  town they are thought to have been built  in the Middle Ages as a source of water  for livestock Freiburg in general has a  distinctly medieval feel but despite its  appearance the Old Town is quite new  most of the original buildings were  damaged or destroyed during the war it  took the people of Freiburg decades of  painstaking work to repair and  reconstruct them an impressive testament  to that is the historic merchants hall  originally built in the 14th century and  lovingly restored  the in tomb Houghton Baron is supposedly  the oldest in Germany it's been serving  food and drinks to guests for almost  seven hundred years the menu focuses on  regional specialties  freshly sourced organic products are  very popular in freiburg the fine wines  are likewise from the bottom region in  the alta waha right next to the  cathedral everything revolves around  regional vintages with more than 300  wineries in the region with its  favorable climate modern is known as the  Burgundy paradise of Germany  on warm sunny days in freiburg people  like to sit outdoors the old town offers  many pleasant options for residents and  visitors alike  there are numerous car free zones the  city was already implementing green  principles in the early 1980s a symbol  of that is the local enthusiasm for  cycling it's the perfect way to get  around in the city and it's also ideal  for those who seek recreation in the  surrounding region  that's because there are several hundred  kilometres of bike paths in and around  the city one popular destination is the  Shou in slot a mountain in the nearby  Black Forest there is no need to take a  bike instead you can take the cable car  to an elevation of 1200 meters  once you get to the top the views are  wonderful as far as the eye can see  Sean's Londe is a big hit with winter  sports fans and with summertime hikers  and don't forget Freiburg is a gateway  to the beautiful Black Forest  you
 

